<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- spec §7 — the vault uses SecAccessControl, which forces the
       data-protection keychain, which requires this entitlement. Without it
       SecItemAdd returns errSecMissingEntitlement (-34018).

       Ad-hoc signing accepts the group only when it matches the bundle ID;
       a real team-prefixed group ($(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.aflekkas.pane)
       needs a provisioning profile and a paid account. -->
  <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
  <array>
    <string>com.aflekkas.pane</string>
  </array>

  <!-- spec §7 passkeys. THE key fact (ADR 0003): with this entitlement WebKit's
       own WebAuthn implementation handles navigator.credentials inside
       WKWebView and talks to AuthenticationServices directly. Pane writes NO
       WebAuthn code — no CBOR, no clientDataJSON, no attestation parsing.

       Requesting it is a business step, not an engineering one: macOS 13.3+,
       Apple-reviewed, and Apple's own text requires the Account Holder role on
       an ORGANIZATION developer account (which needs a D-U-N-S number), via
       https://developer.apple.com/contact/request/macos-browsers-passkeys/

       Apple's review criteria also require the app to ALREADY behave as a
       browser — http+https schemes declared, a URL field or search on launch.
       That is why passkeys are last in the build order rather than early:
       the ordering is forced by the review, not by preference.

       Declared here so the plumbing is in place. Without the grant, WebKit
       restricts passkeys to relying parties covered by associated-domains
       below, which is how this gets verified before any approval arrives. -->
  <key>com.apple.developer.web-browser.public-key-credential</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- Verification path pre-grant: a domain we control. The same code then
       widens to every site once the entitlement lands — nothing is stubbed and
       nothing waits. Replace with a real domain when one exists. -->
  <key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
  <array>
    <string>webcredentials:pane.invalid</string>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
